1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:23,400
Lisa, stop!

2
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:35,660
How can you possibly expect to beat us when you have no powers to speak of?

3
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:37,440
You don't have to do this, Lisa!

4
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:44,720
Due to the plague that is human combustion, weak men like you live and die at the mercy of the flames.

5
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:52,680
But through Lisa's compatibility with the bugs, she's kindled the flames within herself.

6
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:56,760
Both of my parents were killed during a fire that was caused by an infernal.

7
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:03,140
After that, I lived in terror until the bug awakened my power and drove my fear away.

8
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,220
These guys are lying to you, Lisa!

9
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:08,200
I don't have any more powers than you did as a kid.

10
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:13,120
And as a fire soldier, I know the terror of the flames as well as anyone.

11
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:15,280
I face it every day!

12
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:21,620
Seems to me that Giovanni wants you to be scared.

13
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:23,960
He's using your fear to control you!

14
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:27,060
You accuse me as you brandish an axe at her.

15
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:28,420
The axe is for you!

16
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:32,460
He doesn't care about you, Lisa!

17
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,640
You have no reason to protect him!

18
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:40,860
The flaming tentacles which envelop me are magnetically attuned, so they move to protect me of their own accord.

19
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:45,000
The flames I used to live in fear of now keep me safe!

20
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:48,440
What kind of bug is able to give people powers like that?

21
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:52,000
Would you like to know?

22
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,100
Well, I'm not killing!

23
00:01:55,100 --> 00:02:00,240
You'll leave this world just as ignorant as you were coming in!

24
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:02,240
You are one annoying old man!

25
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:08,300
Did you actually believe that you could put out my fire with a toy like that?

26
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:11,380
I don't think it's gonna work, Captain!

27
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:12,880
We'll see about that!

28
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:17,380
It seems like this fight is a joke to you.

29
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,800
It's not, I promise.

30
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:23,940
I'm trying my hardest to save you from the flames that hold you captive.

31
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,260
So hang in there!

32
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,620
I am not their captive!

33
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:30,480
If those feelers aren't defending you, why do you look so scared?

34
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,620
I'm not scared, but you should be!

35
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,180
I'm not fighting you!

36
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:38,780
I'm fighting a fire!

37
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:45,500
Fire extinguishers have no place on the field of battle.

38
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,600
You truly are a fool.

39
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:52,560
You've forgotten, but there's a motto we fire soldiers live by.

40
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:54,680
Protect human life and property.

41
00:02:55,840 --> 00:03:00,320
This piece of gear might not be flashy, but it does its job every time.

42
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,660
It saved more lives than I can count!

43
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:06,260
Kill them.

44
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:07,400
Yes, right.

45
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,540
Your naivety will be the death of you.

46
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:16,220
Tell me, how do you plan to keep saving people's lives when you've thrown your own away?

47
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:19,980
Believe it or not, I'm very protective of my life.

48
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:22,660
I'm sorry for making you wait, Lisa.

49
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,160
But everything's in place now.

50
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:30,620
Obi!

51
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:36,360
You took all those hits on purpose, so you could place extinguisher grenades beneath her tentacles!

52
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:42,980
I'm falling.

53
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:47,900
I've lost everything.

54
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,000
Everyone.

55
00:03:50,780 --> 00:03:51,300
Mom.

56
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:51,920
Dad.

57
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:52,980
Dad.

58
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:07,920
Fuck it.

59
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:18,520
You haven't forgotten what you are again, have you, feeler?

60
00:04:37,920 --> 00:05:00,520
Take what you got and leave now, you're wearing out your welcome No one here wants to see you here, yeah Think that you won from day one, once the devil will come You know just why he wants you, don't you?

61
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:15,620
Your crooked desire, it doesn't seem so right Miscuited, divided, at the point of the reason You're starting a fire, you gotta watch it burn Try to save yourself like you always do

62
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:26,740
Every bridge we've built, you think it's just a burning death Just burn it down, when everything is gone

63
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:39,060
You wish you only heard us out, heard us out Screaming, Miscuited, Miscuited

64
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:46,980
Miscuited, Miscuited

65
00:05:46,980 --> 00:06:07,540
It was I who saved you from the fear of the flames I who gave you purpose Vulcan never would have given you a home if not for me You'd best remember the debt you owe Come back here

66
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:20,180
Don't do this I have to, though Back when I had absolutely nothing, Dr. Giovanni came and rescued me I can't leave him now

67
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:25,260
Just try to forget we ever met, okay?

68
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:30,620
Damn you!

69
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:34,860
Take one more step and I'll burn through her neck with this wire

70
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:46,540
Listen well, Vulcan If you want to save her life, you'll do exactly as I say

71
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:50,300
Pick up that gun and shoot Obi

72
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:53,380
You really are a rotten bastard to the core

73
00:06:53,380 --> 00:07:01,460
You should rejoice, Fela Your life is being put to use in the service of the Evangelist right now

74
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:03,460
Isn't that what you want?

75
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:07,500
Vulcan, do as he says

76
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:08,000
Huh?

77
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:18,540
Sorry, sir

78
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:20,240
This isn't your fault

79
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,380
No more stalling

80
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:24,240
Act now or else

81
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:27,420
There's no point in making a big production out of it

82
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:28,860
Just do as I say

83
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:31,040
Shoot and Fela will live

84
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:33,220
Don't and Lisa will die

85
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:35,100
That's all there is to it.

86
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,340
I swear I'm gonna kill you, Giovanni!

87
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:38,540
Are you?

88
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:44,100
Well, before you do, you can watch as my heating wire lops off this poor girl's head.

89
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:46,880
Go ahead. Pull the trigger.

90
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:49,300
It's the only way you can save Lisa.

91
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:54,240
I can't do it.

92
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,360
Then Lisa is finished.

93
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:58,380
Do it, Vulcan! Shoot me!

94
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:00,020
If you don't, he'll kill Lisa.

95
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:02,380
But if I give in, then...

96
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:22,540
You killed your captain and your only chance of winning just to save this girl.

97
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:29,500
Lisa.

98
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:30,900
Captain.

99
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:35,140
Ha ha ha ha ha...

100
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:36,480
Huh?

101
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:38,980
Even knowing I'd be fine, that was scary!

102
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:40,940
Giovanni!

103
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:47,260
That turnout coat isn't made to be bulletproof.

104
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:50,500
So what extra protection did you have?

105
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:54,120
Oh. Would you like to know?

106
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:54,820
Huh?

107
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:56,320
You feeling curious?

108
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:59,320
Well, I'm not gonna tell you!

109
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,320
I gave him a special holistic vest before we came!

110
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:03,320
Hmm...

111
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:06,320
I'm working as the 8th Engineer now!

112
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:09,320
There's no way I'm gonna let my captain fight without protection!

113
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:13,320
Even so, that was a reckless ploy.

114
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:17,320
It's the trust we put into each other that makes the members of Company 8 a real team.

115
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:21,320
Trust? What an absurd, inexplicable concept!

116
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:24,320
Your hardware's a disorganized mess!

117
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:26,320
You're lucky that Pop isn't here to see it!

118
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:29,320
Get ready, dirtbag! Equip penguin mess!

119
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:36,320
Let's see if that machinery of yours can pass a strike test!

120
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:50,320
Your hardware's as weak as it looks!

121
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,320
Lisa!

122
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,320
Lisa!

123
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,320
Good work, I'll take over!

124
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:55,320
Considering your lack of powers, you're managing quite well.

125
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,320
You used to be a fire soldier like me.

126
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:59,320
You were meant to protect people from the flames.

127
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:02,320
Why would you go from saving people to turning them into infernals?

128
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:04,320
What does your evangelist hope to accomplish by spreading so much terror?

129
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:08,320
Earlier you told me that the fire soldier's maxim was to protect human life and property.

130
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,320
Did you not?

131
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:18,320
Tell me, can you really not see how trivial such things are?

132
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,320
Humans are such a small portion of the Earth's energy.

133
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,320
We are vermin scuttling across the planet's crust.

134
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,320
Of course, mankind should burn.

135
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,320
It's the only way to become part of something greater!

136
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,320
I'm on a clap!

137
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,320
About 250 years ago, this planet's surface was torn apart by the great king.

138
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,320
I'm on a clap!

139
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:27,320
I'm on a clap!

140
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:28,320
I'm on a clap!

141
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,320
I'm on a clap!

142
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,320
You're still trying to be the greatest universe of million attentions of all the

143
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:34,320
minds of humans, and we must really not see how trivial such things are.

144
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:39,320
Humans are such a small portion of the Earth's energy.

145
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:42,320
We are vermin scuttling across the planet's crust.

146
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,320
Of course, mankind should burn.

147
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,320
It's the only way to become part of something greater!

148
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:45,320
I'm on a clap!

149
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:51,320
About 250 years ago, this planet's surface was torn apart by the great cataclysm.

150
00:10:51,320 --> 00:11:00,120
This catastrophe was caused by the sudden release of an immense Adola Burst, and the place that Adola Burst came from is one you know.

151
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:03,720
It's a place you believe in, if you have faith.

152
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:15,860
Long before the solar calendar began, before the Great Cataclysm, since time immemorial, humankind has lived in perpetual fear of this place.

153
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:24,860
Regardless of what causes spontaneous human combustion, I'll do my damndest to stop it. You still haven't made a case for burning people alive.

154
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:31,700
Spontaneous human combustion is a part of the natural order. Would you defy the laws of nature?

155
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:34,160
The bugs you use are made by people!

156
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:45,160
Do you earnestly believe that the Evangelist is no more than a regular person?

157
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:52,700
It doesn't matter what the Evangelist really is. Your cult wanted an idol to worship, so you prop one up for yourselves.

158
00:11:52,700 --> 00:12:02,080
Honestly, what a ridiculous notion. You say that we worship an idol, then what's the great sun god of the Holy Soul Temple?

159
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:08,780
Why bother offering prayers that you don't know will be answered to a god that you don't know exists?

160
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:12,720
Yeah? Well, at least the temple doesn't go around roasting people.

161
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:16,120
The Evangelist is no mere idol.

162
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:23,160
A powerless man such as yourself cannot comprehend what the Evangelist is.

163
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:29,120
But that truth is likely beginning to dawn on your soldier, Shinra Kusakabe.

164
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:46,060
You good, Shinra? Talk to me.

165
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:14,240
Where am I?

166
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:16,880
What is this?

167
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,120
Who...

168
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,020
Who are you?

169
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:36,240
Shinra?

170
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:54,500
Show?

171
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:54,800
Show?

172
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:17,440
Shira?

173
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,640
You okay?

174
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:20,640
What happened?

175
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:21,640
I...

176
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:27,640
I don't know.

177
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:32,200
What's the matter?

178
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:39,320
Do you see something?

179
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:40,440
It's Sho.

180
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:47,640
He's up ahead, waiting.

181
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:53,280
As we speak, Shinra Kusakabe's Adola Burst will be getting stronger through his link with

182
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:55,280
Commander Sho.

183
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,280
Link?

184
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,960
How exactly are they connected?

185
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:00,840
What is an Adola Burst, really?

186
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:07,200
It is a special flame, belonging to those who have become more than pyrokinetics.

187
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:11,840
It affects all forms of heat, and it's the spark from which infernals spring.

188
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:16,520
You're saying that an Adola Burst like Shinra's are what make infernals?

189
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:19,400
Then what are those bugs you people use?

190
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:22,840
You wish to know how they relate.

191
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:28,840
Insects took a drastically different evolutionary path than the rest of the animal kingdom.

192
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:32,520
Which begs the question, where do bugs come from?

193
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:37,200
Some say it's the same place as the Adola Burst.

194
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,840
Like moths to a flame.

195
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:46,840
Perhaps every burnt insect is a child who tried to find its mother.

196
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:58,840
So you came after all, Shinra Kusakabe?

197
00:15:58,840 --> 00:15:59,840
Yeah.

198
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,880
I came here to keep my promise.

199
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:05,120
You say you made a vow, Knave.

200
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,120
To whom?

201
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,120
To Mom.

202
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:08,840
The woman who loved us both.

203
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:13,840
I have but one mother figure in my life, and that is the Evangelist.

204
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:17,840
The thought that you're my brother turns my stomach.

205
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:18,840
How can that be?

206
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:21,840
I was not born from some filthy womb.

207
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:39,840
Don't talk about Mom like that.

208
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:44,840
I'm about to watch two Adola Bursts go flame to flame.

209
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:46,840
This is awesome!

210
00:16:46,840 --> 00:17:03,840
The end, please!

211
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:33,820
Oh, my God.

212
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:40,560
Here I was hoping we could catch up a bit.

213
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:07,640
You saw that, too.

214
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:44,500
That wasn't just fast.

215
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:46,720
It was like he stopped time.

216
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:49,040
How can a pyrokinetic do that?

217
00:18:49,040 --> 00:19:11,080
Hey, Captain!

218
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:12,900
Lieutenant Hinoa!

219
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:13,460
Maki!

220
00:19:13,940 --> 00:19:15,040
Found you!

221
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:17,660
This lesson is over.

222
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:22,640
My task was to get Shinra Kusukabe to Commander Shou.

223
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:25,300
Now that this objective has been accomplished,

224
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:28,700
I have no need to stall for any more time.

225
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:32,520
All is in accordance with the will of the Evangelist.

226
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:33,500
Hold it!

227
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:40,620
So Adola Bursts are the cause of human combustion, huh?

228
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,720
What the hell is happening to the world right now?

229
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:47,860
Yeah, just keep walking!

230
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,440
I'll leave Lisa with you.

231
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:53,600
But you will never reverse her conditioning.

232
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:55,580
Please don't leave me behind.

233
00:19:55,580 --> 00:19:57,600
I'll do anything you told me to.

234
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:58,540
I'll be good.

235
00:19:59,460 --> 00:19:59,840
Lisa!

236
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:02,680
Faith.

237
00:20:03,300 --> 00:20:03,900
Religion.

238
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:05,560
Brainwashing.

239
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:08,940
The ailments mankind could never cure.

240
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:13,580
Farewell.

241
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:19,480
It doesn't matter how swiftly you can move.

242
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:21,880
You will never be able to match me, Knave.

243
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:25,620
The fact is that you and I exist in two separate universes.

244
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,160
Universes?

245
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:28,120
Hold on.

246
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:29,640
What are you saying?

247
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:32,060
That you're on a different level than me?

248
00:20:32,380 --> 00:20:34,100
So you think I should just give up?

249
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:38,120
I'm taking you home if I had to drag you kicking and screaming!

250
00:20:38,120 --> 00:21:07,500
You play tag kind of rough, little bro.

251
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:12,300
The universe has time freezing.

252
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:16,120
If he's engaging enough heat to expand the whole universe...

253
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:17,700
No.

254
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,360
That can't be.

